# Performance Hub — Nightly (V2)

**Deliverable:** the live site at `https://gtl-ops-652.github.io/GTL-652G-1-89-1-18/hub/`, refreshed with data through **yesterday**, byte-for-byte the v7_4_4 design (DESIGN_V="7_4_4" gate). One artifact copy to `/mnt/user-data/outputs/` as failure insurance. Nothing else.

**Trigger:** chat phrase `run performance hub`, or the nightly scheduled task. **This is an unattended run: no pauses, no clarifying questions, no "want me to publish?" — go start to finish.**

**V2 changes from V1:** (a) `WINDOW_RIGHT` = **yesterday** (today − 1) — the old today − 2 lag buffer is removed everywhere; (b) **one window rule** — every const, every tab, every pull is anchored to the same `WINDOW_RIGHT` computed once at run start, FIN included; (c) **anti-stale guard** — every spliced const is verified changed from template baseline; a const that survives at baseline is a failed rebuild and blocks publish; (d) cross-tab date-consistency verification added to the publish gate.

---

## 0 · What this skill DOES NOT touch

### TEMPLATE SOURCE OF TRUTH = THE REPO. NOT this skill folder. NOT project knowledge. NOT memory.

The presentation layer is **FROZEN** in the repo at **`hub/template.html`** (StatiCrypt-encrypted with the shared hub login) with plaintext integrity manifest **`hub/template.manifest.json`**. Fetch procedure, every run:

1. GET `hub/template.html` and `hub/template.manifest.json` from `GTL-Ops-652/GTL-652G-1-89-1-18` via the authenticated Contents API (`?ref=main`, base64-decode) — never `raw.githubusercontent.com` (CDN cache).
2. Decrypt the template with the shared login (password `winbranchoftheyear`, salt `38cb82b98561283c7ba6c6c8400a5d9a`) using staticrypt's own lib (`npm install staticrypt@3.5.4`; `lib/cryptoEngine.js` `hashPassword` + `lib/codec.js` `decode`).
3. **HARD GATE — all three must pass or STOP, do not publish, surface to Stephen:** (a) `sha256(decrypted plaintext)` equals `plaintext_sha256` in the manifest; (b) the plaintext contains `DESIGN_V="` matching the manifest's `design_v` (currently `7_4_4`); (c) exactly 16 unique `/*<<DATA:NAME>>*/` markers.
4. **NEVER rebuild the hub from project knowledge, skill-folder copies, older commits, or memory.** If the repo template is unreachable or fails the gate, the run STOPS — a skipped night is recoverable; a design regression published to the live site is not (this has happened twice: 7/19 and 7/20 nightly runs clobbered supervised weekend builds by improvising from stale copies).

**Why the repo and not this folder:** writes to `/mnt/skills/user/` during a chat session do NOT persist into the fresh container a scheduled run gets — the folder resets to the last *installed* skill package. The repo is persistent, versioned, and reachable by every run with the PAT.

**Re-freeze procedure (supervised design changes only):** in the same session as the design change — (a) StatiCrypt-encrypt the new plaintext template (markers intact, locked salt), PUT to `hub/template.html`; (b) update `hub/template.manifest.json` (`design_v`, `plaintext_sha256`, `frozen` date, notes); (c) verify both by re-GET + hash compare; (d) if `DESIGN_V` changed, update this SKILL.md's gate value AND hand Stephen the updated skill package to re-install — a SKILL.md edited only in the session folder will silently revert.

The template contains the full page — head, CSS, the KPI Focus Loop engine, the Action Jackson card engine, all renderers and wiring — with **16 data-const markers** of the form `/*<<DATA:NAME>>*/const NAME=…;/*<</DATA:NAME>>*/`.

The nightly run regenerates ONLY those 16 consts and splices them back in. **Never edit the engine, renderers, markup, CSS, or the WIN ix mappings.** Any layout/behavior change is a separate, supervised task that re-freezes the template — not this job.

The 16 consts: `S1 S4 ONE_STAR DRIVE_S S5 S6 S7 S8 MEM SAM ROSTER SM_TRADE FIN PR GOAL WIN`.

> **One-time template audit (COMPLETE — v7_4_4 verified clean 2026-07-20; retained for reference only):** confirm that every rendered date range on every tab — Vitals/Pace, KPI trends, Service Managers, Technicians, Watch List — derives from the `WIN` const (or FIN/PR-driven labels), with **no date text hard-coded in the frozen HTML**. If any tab's label is literal text, that tab will show stale dates no matter what this skill does; flag it to Stephen for a supervised template re-freeze. Once confirmed clean, this audit is done and never repeats.

