## 1 · Source of truth (read FRESH every run — never from memory)

Formulas, targets, thresholds, roster rules, SQL, attribution, and file pins are NOT in this skill. **One source of truth: `Unified_KPI_Source_Map.md` in SharePoint `Claude Docs/Alita/`** — open by pinned itemId, discover by folder-listing, never `sharepoint_search`. Read it fresh every run. It is authoritative for every section below and **wins over any older per-task map wherever they conflict** (it carries Stephen's current rulings — % Jobs Reviewed 12%, channel goals $1.2M / $800K / $400K, the `review_bk` distinct-key lock, the membership-flag trap, etc.).

The hub is the only output that needs **both attribution levels**, and the map supplies both — this is exactly why the map beats the Action Jackson map (which is tech/SM only):
- **Tech / SM level** (map §4 + the tech-level variants in §5) → the Service Manager cards, Technicians table, Watch List. Roster / SM attribution / membership from the ServiceTitan report (§3c); per-tech KPIs from Databricks (§5.x tech variants).
- **Trade / branch level** (map §4 + the trade/branch variants in §5) → the `FIN` object behind the Branch pace cards: revenue §5.1, channels §5.2, reviews §5.5, membership §5.6, completed jobs §5.10 — all at trade/branch.

Everything operational also comes from the map: Genie discipline (§2), ServiceTitan report parsing + Team→SM map (§3c), Samsara selection + tech→trade mapping (§3b/§5.9), attribution + schema-column locks (§4), and all rate targets (§6b).

**`GOAL` / goals file:** per map §6a — read the pinned **`Yearly Goals.xlsx`** (Claude Docs **root**; itemId in map §1) fresh each run. While the Excel's Reviews/Memberships rows stay empty, apply interim **400/mo reviews · 300/mo memberships** with a Verification-Notes flag until Stephen fills them. (The `2026 Goals.xlsx` in Alita is a byte-identical copy; the map points the hub at the **root** file so all five dashboards read the same goals — do not point the hub at the Alita copy unless the root file is retired and the map's §1/§6a pin is updated to match.)

**Executable machinery:** for the runnable *implementation* — the Genie call flow, xlsx/CSV parsing, roster-resolution code, itemId recovery, and the publish sub-steps — reuse `task-action-jackson-sm-performance` (V2) verbatim. The Unified map governs all formulas, filters, targets, and pins; the AJ skill only supplies the code that executes them. Shared publish config (repo `GTL-Ops-652/GTL-652G-1-89-1-18`, token, StatiCrypt password + locked salt, encrypt/publish guards) is mirrored in map §2; the hub's own path is `hub/index.html` (§5 below).

