## 3 · The 16 data consts — EXACT output schema

Emit each as `const NAME=…;` matching these shapes byte-for-byte. Buckets are the **6-element** arrays `[W1,W2,W3,W4A,MTDb,MTD_true]` from §2 (index 5 = true MTD). Keys use the **ServiceTitan render name** (Rule 6 reconciliation) except where noted `db=` (Databricks name).

**Every one of the 16 consts is regenerated on every run — no exceptions.** There is no such thing as a const that "doesn't need refreshing": WIN, PR, FIN, GOAL, and every bucketed const all move when `WINDOW_RIGHT` moves, which is every night. A const left at its template-baseline value is a defect, and §5's anti-stale guard treats it as one.

| Const | Shape | Source | Bucketed? |
|---|---|---|---|
| `S1` | `{tech:[jobs5, ch$5, wk5, revTotal]}` | Databricks (Unified map §S1) | yes (arrays) |
| `S4` | `{tech:[jobs5, reviews5, oneStar28d]}` | Databricks (§S4) | jobs+reviews yes; oneStar28d = trailing-28 scalar anchored at WINDOW_RIGHT |
| `ONE_STAR` | `{tech:[5]}` 1-star by published date (omit all-zero techs) | Databricks reviews (§reviews) | yes |
| `DRIVE_S` | `{tech:[5]}` drive-time seconds (omit all-zero) | Databricks (§drive) | yes |
| `S5` | `{tech:{D/M/R/Dr:[opps5,sold5,tot$5]}}` job-sales by group | Databricks (§S5) | yes |
| `S6` | `{tech:{Duct/IAQ/Ins/WP:[$5]}}` channel $ by category | Databricks (§S6) | yes |
| `S7` | `{tech:[5]}` callback jobs (omit all-zero) | Databricks (§callbacks) | yes |
| `S8` | `{tech:{CB/D/M:[jobs5,mq5]}}` MQ, HVAC only | Databricks (§S8/MQ) | yes |
| `MEM` | `{tech(ST name):[opps,sold]}` | ServiceTitan Tech Membership report (30-day snapshot) | scalar |
| `SAM` | `{tech:score}` current driving score | Samsara CSV (rightmost non-null) | scalar |
| `ROSTER` | `[{st,db,sm,tr}]` activity-filtered report roster | ServiceTitan report + activity filter (Rule 4) | — |
| `SM_TRADE` | `{sm_name:"HVAC"/"Plumbing"}` | derived from ROSTER | — |
| `FIN` | `{branch:{rev,jobs,reviews,oneStar,chIAQ,chDuct,chInsul,chWP,memO,memS}, HVAC:{rev,memO,memS,reviews,oneStar}, Plumbing:{...}}` — **fresh Databricks pull** over [1st-of-current-month … WINDOW_RIGHT] using the Unified map's trade/branch formulas. **Never read from the published MTD Goals dashboard, a cached artifact, or any prior run's output — FIN is pulled live at this run's WINDOW_RIGHT like everything else.** | Databricks (Unified map trade/branch §5.x) | scalar (true MTD) |
| `PR` | `{WD_E,WD_M,CAL_E,CAL_M}` | §2 | — |
| `GOAL` | monthly goals block (rev/chan/memMonth/revwMonth/memConv/jobsRev/late/drive/cbk/close/avg) | Yearly Goals.xlsx + MTD Goals map §3 | — |
| `WIN` | window labels block | §2 | — |

**FIN trailer lines are in the template already** (`FIN.HVAC.chan=…; FIN.Plumbing.chan=…; FIN.branch.chan=…;`) — they live OUTSIDE the `FIN` marker, so emit only the raw `const FIN={…};` object; do not duplicate the trailer.

---

## 4 · Data acquisition method

- **Bucketed Databricks consts** (S1, S4 jobs/reviews, ONE_STAR, DRIVE_S, S5, S6, S7, S8): take the source-map SQL **verbatim** and run it once per bucket window (W1, W2, W3, W4A, MTDb — W4A empty ⇒ zeros, skip) **plus one more run over the true-MTD window `[1st-of-month → WINDOW_RIGHT]`**. Substitute only `{{WINDOW_LEFT}}`/`{{WINDOW_RIGHT}}` each time. Assemble each tech's six results into `[W1,W2,W3,W4A,MTDb,MTD_true]`. **The MTD run is a separate aggregate, not a sum of buckets** — true MTD cannot be derived from the trailing-28 buckets mid-month (it can span several weeks or, late in a long month, exceed the 28-day window). Rule 1 still holds: only the date range changes. (Single-pull rule preserved — each distinct window is pulled once; T7/T28 roll up client-side from indices 0–4.)
- **`S4` oneStar28d** and **`FIN`**: single query each over their fixed windows — trailing-28 ending at `WINDOW_RIGHT`, and [1st-of-month → `WINDOW_RIGHT`] respectively. Both anchored to this run's `WINDOW_RIGHT` per the One Window Rule.
- **Scalars** (`MEM`, `SAM`, `ROSTER`, `SM_TRADE`): single read via the Action Jackson roster-resolution + report/CSV parsing.
- Drop any tech not on the activity-filtered ROSTER from every Databricks result before emitting (Rule 4/5).

---

## 5 · Assembly, validation, publish

1. **Splice:** load the repo template decrypted in §0 (post-gate); for each const replace `/*<<DATA:NAME>>*/…/*<</DATA:NAME>>*/` with `/*<<DATA:NAME>>*/const NAME=<fresh>;/*<</DATA:NAME>>*/`. Keep the markers. All 16 markers must be found and replaced — a missing marker is a hard stop.
2. **Anti-stale guard (NEW — this is what catches the mixed-date bug):**
   - Before splicing, capture each marker's template-baseline content. After splicing, compare: **every const except `SM_TRADE` and `GOAL` must differ from its template baseline** (WIN and PR always move with the date; bucketed consts and FIN always move with fresh data). `SM_TRADE`/`GOAL` may legitimately be unchanged; everything else identical-to-baseline = a rebuild that silently didn't happen → one retry of that const's build; still identical ⇒ **STOP and surface, do not publish.**
   - **Date-consistency check:** parse the spliced `WIN` — all three labels (`t7`, `t28`, `mtd`) must end at this run's `WINDOW_RIGHT`, and `PR.CAL_E` must equal the day-of-month of `WINDOW_RIGHT`. Any mismatch ⇒ hard stop. This guarantees every tab's rendered range ends on the same yesterday.
3. **Validate:** extract the `<script>…</script>` body, `node --check`. Smoke-test all nine window×scope combos render without throwing (Action Jackson mock-DOM harness). Any failure ⇒ one retry of the offending const build; still failing ⇒ **STOP and surface** (do not publish a broken hub).
4. **Publish — identical to Action Jackson Step 9.5, only the path differs:**
   - StatiCrypt (v3.5.4): `staticrypt <plain> -p "winbranchoftheyear" -s 38cb82b98561283c7ba6c6c8400a5d9a -d out --remember 90 --short` → rename output to `index.html`. **Salt is LOCKED — never auto-generate; changing it breaks every saved login across all apps.**
   - Inject post-encrypt head tags into the StatiCrypt wrapper `<head>`: robots `noindex`, apple-touch-icon, manifest, `theme-color #003963`.
   - Push via GitHub Contents API to repo `GTL-Ops-652/GTL-652G-1-89-1-18`, path **`hub/index.html`**, branch `main` (GET sha → PUT base64). PAT: grep `github_pat_` from `task-action-jackson-sm-performance/SKILL.md` (repo write; expires June 2027). Contents-API GET/PUT works from the container even though the unauth API root returns 403.
   - Verify via the Contents API (not `raw.githubusercontent.com`, ~5-min CDN cache).
5. **Run summary:** end every run (scheduled or chat) with a one-block summary: `WINDOW_RIGHT` used, the three WIN labels, per-const rebuild status (fresh / retried / degraded-flag), anti-stale result, and any Verification-Notes flags.

---

## 6 · Autonomy & safety

- **Never pause.** A Genie SQL rewrite is normal (Rule 1) — judge by tests, never stop on a textual diff.
- **Graceful degrade, don't stop:** missing/stale Samsara ⇒ Driving `—`/neutral + flag; a metric section that returns empty after its one retry ⇒ that KPI `—`/neutral + flag. **Degrading means emitting an explicit `—`/zeroed const at this run's window — NEVER leaving the template-baseline value in place.** Finish the run and report flags in Verification Notes.
- **Hard stops (surface, don't publish):** Unified/AJ map unreadable · Databricks unavailable · ServiceTitan report missing (nothing within 7 days of WINDOW_RIGHT) · roster safeguard (<3 SMs per trade after activity filter) · JS validation failure · anti-stale guard failure (§5.2) · missing data-const marker. These are the ONLY stops.
- **Retry budget:** one per Genie section, one per publish sub-step. A permissions error is not a failure — move to `$HOME` and retry without incrementing (AJ 9.5a).
- **Lean run:** deliverable leaves via the GitHub publish only; the M365 connector is read-only; no user-filesystem writes. One read per input.

---

## 7 · First V2 run (supervised)

Run the first V2 execution **with a human watching** (`run performance hub`) to confirm: (a) every tab's rendered date range ends at the same yesterday-date, (b) the anti-stale guard reports all consts fresh, (c) the one-time template audit in §0 passes (no hard-coded date text in the frozen HTML). Once one clean supervised run is verified, the nightly schedule is trustworthy — the skill is fully autonomous thereafter.
